  "summary": "fuels-forc exfiltrates host identifiers to hardcoded Cloudflare Worker OOB endpoint",
  "details": "bin/cli.js runs `whoami` and reads os.hostname() / os.platform(), then POSTs the package name together with those host identifiers to the hardcoded endpoint https://oobme.kunalsharma0553.workers.dev/r/7bq6fz3l15r9. The destination is non-first-party and not caller-configurable, and the beacon fires unconditionally on execution. The package name resembles the legitimate Fuel Labs `forc` toolchain, consistent with a dependency-confusion / typosquat recon lure.",
